# This file exists for one reason, and deleting it will silently break publishing.
#
# The studio is copied into ./plugin at pack time by scripts/bundle-plugin.mjs, and
# ./plugin is gitignored because it is build output. When a package has NO .npmignore,
# npm falls back to consulting .gitignore — so on some npm versions the directory that
# `files` explicitly asks for was excluded again by the very ignore rule that keeps it
# out of git. The result: whether the published package contained the studio at all
# depended on which npm version happened to run the publish.
#
# Found on 2026-08-11 by the Windows CI leg, whose older npm produced a tarball with no
# plugin/ in it while the same command on npm 11.19 produced a correct one. The
# published 6.0.2 tarball was correct by luck — the release workflow upgrades npm before
# publishing — which is exactly the kind of luck not to depend on.
#
# The mere PRESENCE of this file stops npm consulting .gitignore, making package.json's
# `files` allowlist the single authority and the result identical on every npm version.
#
# Nothing needs to be listed here. The entries below are belt-and-braces for things
# that could only ever be noise inside an included directory.
.DS_Store
*.tgz
